$ PSHELL with MID4 vs. the unsymmetric PCOMP it represents. Two identical disconnected cantilever strips:
$ grids 1xx = PCOMP [0/45/-45/90] (PID 1), grids 2xx = PSHELL with MID1/MID2/MID3/MID4 (PID 2) from classical lamination
$ theory (G4 = -B/T^2). Element material angle THETA = 30 deg on both. Corresponding grids must displace identically.
